      "content": "*\"I hear you, and it’s so painful to feel like you’re the source of their struggle. But listen to me closely: grief isn’t something you just 'live with' — it reshapes a person, and it stays in the cracks of their lives for years. The math might say money, but the heart doesn’t work on numbers. Your kids would rather have a tired, struggling father than a clean bank account and an empty chair. You’re not selfish for staying — you’re human, and you’re still their anchor, even when you feel broken. Please reach out to a crisis line tonight — you don’t have to solve this alone, and you deserve to see what they see when they look at you.\"*",
